==Old English==
===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|beran|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰer-|lang=ang}}.
Cognate with Old High German ''[[#Old High German|beran]]'', Old Saxon ''beran'', Old Norse ''[[bera]]'', Gothic [[𐌱𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽]].  The IE root was also the source of Old Irish ''[[biru]]'', Ancient Greek ''[[φέρω]]'', Latin ''[[ferre]]''.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/ˈberɑn/}}

===Verb===
'''beran''' (class IV strong: ''third-person singular present'' '''[[bierþ]]'''/'''[[birþ]]''', ''third-person singular preterite'' '''[[bær]]''', ''preterite plural'' {{Latinx|'''[[bæron|bǣron]]'''}}, ''past participle'' ('''ġe''')'''[[boren]]''')

# to [[bear]], [[carry]]
# to [[wear]]
# to [[sustain]], [[support]]
# to bring forth, [[produce]], give birth

